  "_note": "Map v5's parody brands (MAP_README.md, 'Brands and parodies'; map/model/brands.ts). Every chain the map data names — by its brand's Wikidata ID first, then its brand or name — is drawn as the parody here instead: an invented name, its own colours and logo (made in the game from logo.shape and logo.mark, or replaced by assets/brands/<id>.svg when there is one), and a site template (drive-thru, petrol, supermarket, big box, food). `real` lists only what detection matches against and what the bake's fuzzy check keeps every parody name away from — it is never drawn. Parody rules: no real name or near-spelling (the bake fails on a parody name within tests.brandSimilarity of any real brand name here or in the name-suggestion-index), an original logo, clearly different colours, no slogans, mascots or trade dress; recognisable by what's sold, the site's layout and where it is. ipNote says why each is safe. To add a chain: an entry with its Wikidata ID (the name-suggestion-index lists them: nsi.min.json, brand:wikidata), its real names, a parody built by those rules, and its IP note; bake again.",
